### Requests for the IntelliJ HTTP client (or copy them as curl commands).
### Start the app first: ./mvnw spring-boot:run

### List all users
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users

### Create a user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "ada",
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "fullName": "Ada Lovelace"
}

### Get one user
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/1

### Delete a user
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/users/1

### Content negotiation: ask for JSON -> 200 with a JSON body
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users
Accept: application/json

### Content negotiation: ask for XML -> 406 Not Acceptable (no XML converter until you add jackson-dataformat-xml)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users
Accept: application/xml

### Invalid input -> 400 Bad Request
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "",
  "email": "not-an-email"
}

### Same email twice -> 409 Conflict (run "Create a user" first)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "ada2",
  "email": "ada@example.com"
}

### Unknown id -> 404 Not Found
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/999

### Is the app (and its database) healthy?
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/health

### Every bean in the container
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/beans

### How many HTTP requests have we served?
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/metrics/http.server.requests
